= The Wanderer into the Void

On 26 May the French shot Albert Leo Schlageter on the Golzheimer Heath outside Düsseldorf for blowing up a railway line. He was a Freikorps veteran of the Baltic and of the Ruhr in 1920, and the nationalists have made him a saint.

On 20 June, before the enlarged Executive in Moscow, Karl Radek calls him a courageous soldier of the counter-revolution and a wanderer into the void. If the nationalist youth want to fight for Germany, Radek says, they should fight beside the workers. [? if e23_sch_directive = 1 : A week later the Executive's instruction arrives over his signature. ?]

- @follow: Take the campaign to the nationalist students.
- @refuse: Refuse it.

@follow
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A few hundred recruits from the right. Our own internationalists are disgusted.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('moscow_orders');
RG.comply(45);
Q.e23_schlageter = 1;
Q.independence -= 6;
Q.spd_relation -= 6;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 8;
!}

Our speakers share platforms with Count Reventlow's men in Berlin and Jena. [? if offensive_gone = 0 : Ruth Fischer tells völkisch students that whoever fights Jewish capital is already a fighter of the class war, words the Left will later prefer to forget. ?] The SPD prints the speeches beside Hitler's.

@refuse
subtitle: More independence. Radek is offended.
on-arrival: {!
RG.defy();
Q.e23_schlageter = 2;
Q.independence += 8;
Q.spd_relation += 3;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
!}

[? if luxemburg_alive = 1 : Rosa Luxemburg's reply to Radek runs to three columns and begins: "There is no such thing as a revolutionary nationalism." ?][? if luxemburg_alive = 0 : The Zentrale declares that it will not compete with the nationalists for the memory of a saboteur. ?]
